corrections.new_value:
TV styles nested LineworkModifier owners in the Layout Editor through three pieces:
- a ModelLayers config group (Layer__CategoryKey TrueVision__LineworkModifier__*, SketchUp tags 76-79, Group__AlwaysShow);
- Viewport2d__Frame importing Na__PlCfg__GetLineworkModifiers for widths;
- Viewport2d__Linework treating modifier keys as never top-level.
Without these, VV segments would carry owner keys with no style row and draw in the fallback style.

VV's GLBs come from the same exporter. ValeVision Cloud Sync calls Na__TrueVision__GlbBuilderUtility through 04__Plugin__SyncFeatures/03__GlbExportBridge/Na__ValeVisionCloudSync__GlbExportBridge__.rb:57, and that builder writes nested LineworkModifier nodes (Na__TrueVision__GlbBuilder__EngineCore__LineworkModelHandling__.rb:15, 76). Whether Vale models actually carry tags 76-79 is still unverified.

